# Preview input test-signing prototype

The source was recovered from the original command records. The complete
signature, notice admission, installation and Control bridge sequence
requires a new Linux acceptance run in the scheduled delivery window.

The base-notice archive is a candidate read from the cached pinned Python
image. Its full archive was held in temporary storage and needs fresh
readback. The original transcript records 106 Debian and CPython notices.
The fixture source uses a private test scope marker for first-party code.
It grants no redistribution approval. Formal source and binary notices
remain release inputs.

Both Linux host wrappers acquire /run/lock/ownsolid-heavy.lock followed by
/root/lane-sci-tools/heavy-test.lock and recheck memory, disk and I/O pressure.
Run only after the accepted ARC audit58 and GW qualification windows. The
REL-108 timer continuation has first priority in the delivery window.

Use the restored replay script only when a separately approved window and
the exact source checkout are available. Confirm its recorded source
matches the remote checkout. The test generates an ephemeral Ed25519 key.
No production key is needed. Resolve the exact Qwen LICENSE from its
catalogue pin before running replay.sh.

retained_inputs.py is the smaller read-only path. Run it in an isolated
network namespace with strace restricted to network syscalls. It checks
the protected contracts and retained wheel and notice bytes without
starting an interpreter environment, container or service.

The retained-input transcript ends with a Git status failure caused by
the fixture's 256 MiB address-space limit being inherited by Git.
The archive checks and empty network trace completed successfully before
that command. cleanup-check.log records the separate successful source
and directory check. The runtime/signing prototype has separate pending
acceptance.

Run the prototype after its window is assigned using
`bash replay.sh "$clean_checkout" "$accepted_audit58_commit"`.
Provide the catalogue-matching Qwen LICENSE as qwen-license beside the
script. Its SHA-256 is
832dd9e00a68dd83b3c3fb9f5588dad7dcf337a0db50f7d9483f310cd292e92e.
